.TH XUR.STD 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std \- overview of Xur's standard library
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B std
module is Xur's standard library, registered automatically at startup.
Each submodule is loaded lazily on first
.BR use .
.SH MODULES
.TP
.B std::io
Console I/O.
.BR println ,
.BR eprintln ,
.BR print ,
.BR eprint ,
and
.B readln
for reading a line from stdin.
.TP
.B std::io::c
ANSI colour helpers.
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR blue ,
.BR magenta ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR bold ,
.BR dim .
.TP
.B std::fs
Filesystem access.
.BR read_bytes ,
.BR read_text ,
.BR write_bytes ,
.BR write_text ,
and
.BR exists .
.TP
.B std::process
Run external programs.
.B spawn(program, args)
returns a handle with
.BR wait ,
.BR stdout ,
and
.BR stderr .
.TP
.B std::thread
Threads.
.B spawn(closure)
returns a join handle;
.B sleep(ms)
pauses the current thread.
.TP
.B std::sync
Synchronisation primitives.
.B Mutex
wraps a value with
.B lock()
and
.BR try_lock() .
.B Channel
provides
.B send()
and
.BR recv() .
.TP
.B std::net
Networking.
.B TcpStream
(connect, read, write) and
.B TcpListener
(bind, accept).
.TP
.B std::math
Mathematical functions:
.BR abs ,
.BR floor ,
.BR ceil ,
.BR sqrt ,
.BR pow ,
.BR min ,
.BR max ,
.BR PI ,
.BR E .
.TP
.B std::any
Runtime type introspection.
.B name_of::<T>()
returns a type's name as a string.
.TP
.B std::reflect
Reflection.
.BR fields ,
.BR get ,
.BR set ,
.BR call ,
.BR variants .
Inspect and manipulate structs and enums at runtime.
.TP
.B std::re
Reverse engineering toolkit. See
.BR xur.std.re (7).
.TP
.B std::list
List utilities:
.BR map ,
.BR filter ,
.BR fold ,
.BR zip ,
.BR flat_map ,
.BR sort ,
.BR sort_by ,
.BR rev ,
.BR range .
.TP
.B std::bytes
Byte buffer operations.
.BR zeroed ,
.BR from_list ,
.BR read_u8 / u16 / u32 / u64 ,
.BR write_u8 / u16 / u32 / u64
(little-endian).
.TP
.B std::str
String utilities:
.BR split ,
.BR join ,
.BR trim ,
.BR starts_with ,
.BR ends_with ,
.BR contains ,
.BR replace ,
.BR to_upper ,
.BR to_lower .
.TP
.B std::mem
Struct layout, binary conversion and page allocation.
.BR size_of ,
.BR align_of ,
.BR to_bytes ,
.BR from_bytes ,
.BR alloc_page ,
.BR protect ,
.BR write_bytes ,
.BR free_page .
Includes the
.B Protection
bitwise flags enum.
See
.BR xur.std.mem (7).
.TP
.B std::num
Integer and float methods (available on values directly):
.BR abs ,
.BR pow ,
.BR min ,
.BR max ,
.BR to_float ,
.BR to_hex ,
.BR to_string ,
.BR sqrt ,
.BR floor ,
.BR ceil ,
.BR round ,
.BR to_int .
.TP
.B std::fmt
Format strings.
.B format(template, args...)
returns a formatted string.
.TP
.B std::http
HTTP client.
.BR get ,
.BR post ,
.BR put ,
.BR patch ,
.BR delete ,
.BR head ,
.BR request
(builder).
.B Response
type with
.BR status() ,
.BR text() ,
.BR json() ,
.BR header() ,
.BR headers() .
See
.BR xur.std.http (7).
.TP
.B std::json
JSON serialisation.
.B parse(text)
parses a JSON string into Xur values;
.B stringify(value)
serialises a value to JSON.
.TP
.B std::assert
Test assertions.
.BR is_eq ,
.BR is_ne ,
.BR is_true ,
.BR is_false ,
.BR fail .
.TP
.B std::log
Structured logging via a builder-style subscriber.
.BR subscriber() ,
.BR trace ,
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
.BR error .
See
.BR xur.std.log (7).
.TP
.B std::path
Path manipulation.
.BR join ,
.BR parent ,
.BR file_name ,
.BR stem ,
.BR extension ,
.BR with_extension ,
.BR is_absolute ,
.BR is_relative ,
.BR is_dir ,
.BR is_file ,
.BR exists ,
.BR absolute ,
.BR components .
.TP
.B std::ptr
Raw pointer utilities.
.BR null ,
.BR from_int ,
.BR to_int ,
.BR is_null ,
.BR offset ,
.BR to_hex .
.TP
.B std::cli
Argument parsing (pico-args) and interactive prompts (inquire).
.BR parse ,
.BR table .
.B Args
type with
.BR contains ,
.BR option ,
.BR value ,
.BR subcommand ,
.BR free ,
.BR remaining ,
.BR finish .
Prompts:
.BR prompt ,
.BR confirm ,
.BR select ,
.BR multi_select ,
.BR password ,
.BR editor .
.TP
.B std::time
Monotonic timing.
.B now()
returns an
.B Instant
with
.BR elapsed() ;
.B Duration
has
.BR secs() ,
.BR millis() ,
.BR as_secs_f64() .
Also
.BR sleep() ,
.BR from_secs() ,
.BR from_millis() .
See
.BR xur.std.time (7).
.TP
.B std::regex
Regular expressions.
.B new(pattern)
returns a
.B Regex
with
.BR is_match() ,
.BR find() ,
.BR find_all() ,
.BR captures() ,
.BR replace() ,
.BR replace_all() ,
.BR split() .
See
.BR xur.std.regex (7).
.TP
.B std::xur
Runtime metadata.
.B invoked_by()
returns how the program was launched
.RB ( \(dqcli\(dq " or " \(dqstub\(dq ).
.SH RECORD METHODS
All records support these builtin methods:
.TP
.B fields()
Returns a list of field name strings.
.TP
.B get_field(name)
Returns
.B Some(value)
or
.BR None .
.TP
.B set_field(name, value)
Returns a new record with the field added or replaced.
.TP
.B get_method(name)
Returns
.B Some(fn)
or
.BR None .
.TP
.B set_method(name, fn)
Returns a new record with the method attached.
.SH BUILT-IN FUNCTIONS
These are available without importing
.BR std :
.TP
.B std::import(path)
Dynamically import a module by path at runtime.
.TP
.B std::panic(format, args...)
Stop the program with a formatted runtime error.
.SH PRELUDE
The prelude is loaded into every program automatically and provides:
.TP
.B Option<T>
.BR Some(T) " and " None .
Methods:
.BR unwrap() ,
.BR unwrap_or(default) ,
.BR is_some() ,
.BR is_none() ,
.BR map(f) ,
.BR and_then(f) .
.TP
.B Result<T, E>
.BR Ok(T) " and " Err(E) .
Methods:
.BR unwrap() ,
.BR unwrap_or(default) ,
.BR is_ok() ,
.BR is_err() ,
.BR map(f) ,
.BR map_err(f) ,
.BR and_then(f) .
Supports the
.B ?
operator for early return.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::io;
use std::fs;

fn main() -> Result<(), str> {
    let text = fs::read_text("hello.txt")?;
    io::println("contents: {}", text);
    Ok(())
}
.fi
